{"toolCallId":"call_3d322464d195490590d0b4dcd61b08cb","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/224-deepseek-final2/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n<!-- FILL: Fill the stack row and write three sentences: what changes, where, and how you will prove it. GOOD: Change one bash script. Add one output branch. Prove it with a line count. WEAK: This plan describes the implementation. -->\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., TypeScript, Python 3.11] |\n| **Framework** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., React, FastAPI] |\n| **Storage** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., PostgreSQL, None] |\n| **Testing** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., Jest, pytest] |\n\n### Overview\n[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n<!-- FILL: Turn each gate into a check a command can answer. Keep the boxes unticked until they pass. GOOD: `rg -n 'quiet' recommend-level.sh` prints the new branch before the task starts. WEAK: The team agrees the plan is ready. -->\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [ ] Success criteria measurable\n- [ ] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] Tests passing (if applicable)\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n<!-- FILL: Name the pattern in three words, then list the one component that changes. GOOD: Single script branch. The component is `recommend-level.sh`. WEAK: Standard architecture. -->\n\n### Pattern\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: MVC | MVVM | Clean Architecture | Serverless | Monolith | Other]\n\n### Key Components\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 1]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 2]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n\n### Data Flow\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Brief description of how data moves through the system]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n<!-- FILL: Name each surface the change touches. Write `not a consumer` when it does not read the change. Write `N/A` or delete the whole addendum when no fix surface applies. GOOD: `recommend-level.sh`: owns the output. Action: update. WEAK: Various files. -->\n\nUse this section when `research_intent=fix_bug`, when planning from a deep-review FAIL/CONDITIONAL verdict, or when any finding touches security, path handling, env precedence, schema boundaries, persistence, public responses, or shared policy.\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: producer/helper/policy] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: what owns the behavior] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: update/unchanged/not a consumer] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: grep/test/doc evidence] |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: consumer/status/docs/tests] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: how it observes the behavior] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: update/unchanged/not a consumer] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: grep/test/doc evidence] |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `rg -n '<field|string|helper|literal|error-pattern>' <module-or-files>`.\n- Consumers of changed symbols: `rg -n '<changedSymbol>|<changedConstant>|<changedPublicField>' . --glob '*.ts' --glob '*.js' --glob '*.md'`.\n- Matrix axes: list every independent input axis and the required rows before implementation.\n- Algorithm invariant: for path/redaction/parser/resolver/security fixes, state the invariant and adversarial cases.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n<!-- FILL: Point to `tasks.md` and name the three phases in one line. GOOD: Setup reads the current output. Implementation adds the branch. Verification counts lines. WEAK: See tasks. -->\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n<!-- FILL: Name the one command you will run and the output it must print. GOOD: `--quiet` prints 1 line. The default prints 17. WEAK: Test it manually. -->\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Unit | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Components/functions] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Jest/pytest/etc.] |\n| Integration | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: API endpoints/flows] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Tools] |\n| Manual | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: User journeys] | Browser |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: List each tool the change needs, or write `None`. GOOD: `bash` and `awk`. No new package. WEAK: Usual dependencies. -->\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: System/Library] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Internal/External] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Green/Yellow/Red] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Impact] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n<!-- FILL: Name the trigger and the one command that reverts the change. GOOD: Trigger: the default output changes. Revert the one commit. WEAK: Roll back if needed. -->\n\n- **Trigger**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Conditions requiring rollback]\n- **Procedure**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: How to revert changes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: Draw the phase order in the fence, then fill the table with depends-on and blocks. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Setup to Implementation to Verification. Verification blocks close. WEAK: Phases depend on each other. -->\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Setup) ──────┐\n                      ├──► Phase 2 (Core) ──► Phase 3 (Verify)\nPhase 1.5 (Config) ───┘\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Setup | None | Core, Config |\n| Config | Setup | Core |\n| Core | Setup, Config | Verify |\n| Verify | Core | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n<!-- FILL: Give each phase an estimate and a total. Mark the total as an assumption. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Setup 10 minutes, implementation 30, verification 10. Total 50 minutes. WEAK: A few hours. -->\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Setup | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 1-2 hours] |\n| Core Implementation | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 4-8 hours] |\n| Verification | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 1-2 hours] |\n| **Total** | | **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 6-12 hours]** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n<!-- FILL: Name the trigger, the steps and the data reversal. Write `No` when no data changes. Delete the whole section when the packet ships no deployable service. GOOD: Trigger: default output changes. Steps: revert one commit, rerun the two commands. WEAK: Roll back if needed. -->\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [ ] Backup created (if data changes)\n- [ ] Feature flag configured\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts set\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Immediate action - e.g., disable feature flag]\n2. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Revert code - e.g., git revert or redeploy previous version]\n3. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Verify rollback - e.g., smoke test critical paths]\n4. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Notify stakeholders - if user-facing]\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Yes/No]\n- **Reversal procedure**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Steps or \"N/A\"]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n<!-- FILL: Draw the component order and fill the matrix with produces and blocks. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Script to test to close. WEAK: Components depend on each other. -->\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│   Phase 1   │────►│   Phase 2   │────►│   Phase 3   │\n│   Setup     │     │    Core     │     │   Verify    │\n└─────────────┘     └──────┬──────┘     └─────────────┘\n                          │\n                    ┌─────▼─────┐\n                    │  Phase 2b │\n                    │  Parallel │\n                    └───────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component A] | None | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | B, C |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component B] | A | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | D |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component C] | A | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | D |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component D] | B, C | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Final] | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n<!-- FILL: Name the longest chain and its total. List what can run in parallel. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Implementation to verification, 40 minutes. Docs run in parallel. WEAK: The critical path is the main path. -->\n\n1. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n2. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n3. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Sum of durations]\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task A] and [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task B] can run simultaneously\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task C] and [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task D] can run after Phase 1\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n<!-- FILL: Name three milestones with a command-checkable success criterion. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: M1: the branch exists. `rg -n quiet` prints it. WEAK: Milestones are tracked. -->\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Setup Complete] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: All dependencies ready] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n| M2 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Core Done] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Main features working] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n| M3 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Release Ready] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: All tests pass] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n<!-- FILL: Write one ADR per decision. Name the context, the choice, the consequence and the rejected option. GOOD: ADR-001: a flag, because callers already pass flags. WEAK: We made a decision. -->\n\n### ADR-001: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Decision Title]\n\n**Status**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Proposed/Accepted/Deprecated]\n\n**Context**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What problem we're solving]\n\n**Decision**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What we decided]\n\n**Consequences**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Positive outcome 1]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Negative outcome + mitigation]\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Option B]: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Why rejected]\n\n---\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"One shell script gains a --quiet option, a shared level-line formatter and one output branch. The default and JSON paths stay byte-identical, proven by a captured baseline diff and the two existing Node test scripts.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash 3.2+ (macOS system bash), bash 5 compatible |\n| **Framework** | None - one shell script |\n| **Storage** | None |\n| **Testing** | `bash -n`, `wc -l`, `diff`, and the two existing Node test scripts |\n\n### Overview\n\nThe change lives in one file. The parser learns one boolean, the level line moves into a shared formatter, and the output dispatch gains one branch between JSON and text. Proof is a line count for the quiet path, a byte diff for the report path, and the two existing Node test scripts that already invoke the script with `--json`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [x] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [x] Success criteria measurable\n- [x] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] Tests passing (if applicable)\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\nSingle-script branch (no application pattern applies)\n\n### Key Components\n- **`recommend-level.sh` argument loop**: parses `--quiet` into a `QUIET` boolean and leaves every existing case untouched.\n- **`format_level_line()`**: the single producer of `Recommended Level: <N> (<Name>)`.\n- **`output_quiet()`**: writes that line once, with no leading blank line.\n- **`output_text()`**: the existing report, unchanged except that its level line now comes from the formatter.\n\n### Data Flow\n\n`argv` -> the parser sets `QUIET` -> scoring, confidence and phase calculation run exactly as before -> dispatch chooses `output_json` when `--json` is set, `output_quiet` when `--quiet` is set, and `output_text` otherwise.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| `recommend-level.sh` (`output_text`) | Owns the report and the level line | update | `diff` of the default output against the pre-change capture is empty |\n| `recommend-level.sh` (`show_help` and the header OPTIONS block) | Documents the option surface | update | `--help` names `--quiet` in the options table and in one example |\n| `.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/speckit-plan.yaml` and `speckit-complete.yaml` | The only in-repo callers; both pass `--json` and parse JSON | not a consumer of `--quiet` | `rg -n \"recommend-level.sh\" .skilled/commands` prints two `--json` invocations |\n| `runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-system.js` and `test-phase-validation.js` | Regression tests that invoke the script with `--json` | unchanged | Both scripts pass before and after the change |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `rg -n \"Recommended Level\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` names one producer today; after the change both call sites go through `format_level_line()`.\n- Consumers of changed symbols: `rg -n \"recommend-level.sh\" --glob '!*.md' .` names two YAML call sites, both using `--json`.\n- Matrix axes: quiet on/off x json on/off x phases on/off, plus the error path.\n- Algorithm invariant: with `QUIET=true` and `JSON_OUTPUT=false`, stdout holds exactly one newline-terminated line. Adversarial cases: a copied leading blank line, a trailing blank line, both flags together, and an invalid-input run.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Unit | None - the script has no unit harness | - |\n| Integration | Flag matrix on the real script: quiet on/off x json on/off x phases on/off | `bash`, `wc`, `diff` |\n| Regression | The two existing Node scripts that invoke `recommend-level.sh` with `--json` | `node cli/tests/test-phase-system.js`, `node cli/tests/test-phase-validation.js` |\n| Manual | `--help` output inspection | Terminal |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| Bash 3.2+ | Internal | Green | The script cannot run; already required today |\n| `wc` and `diff` | External | Green | Line-count and byte-equality checks cannot run; manual inspection remains |\n| Node 22.12+ | Internal | Green | The two regression scripts cannot run; the flag matrix still covers output |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\n- **Trigger**: The default text output or the JSON output differs from the captured baseline.\n- **Procedure**: `git revert <commit>` the single commit that touches `recommend-level.sh`, then re-run the baseline capture and the two regression scripts.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Setup) ──────────┐\n                          ├──► Phase 2 (Implementation) ──► Phase 3 (Verification)\n                          │\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Setup | None | Implementation |\n| Implementation | Setup | Verification |\n| Verification | Implementation | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Setup | Low | 10 minutes |\n| Core Implementation | Low | 30 minutes |\n| Verification | Low | 15 minutes |\n| **Total** | | **~55 minutes (assumption)** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [x] Backup created (if data changes) - no data changes\n- [ ] Feature flag configured - not applicable, the flag is opt-in at the call site\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts set - not applicable, no service\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. Revert the single commit that touches `recommend-level.sh`.\n2. Re-run the baseline capture for `--loc 500 --files 15` and the full-risk variant.\n3. Run the two regression scripts.\n4. No stakeholder notification is needed; the default output never changes.\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** No\n- **Reversal procedure**: N/A\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│   Phase 1   │────►│   Phase 2   │────►│   Phase 3   │\n│   Setup     │     │    Core     │     │   Verify    │\n└─────────────┘     └─────────────┘     └─────────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| Baseline capture (T002) | None | The pre-change output fixtures | T012, T013 |\n| `format_level_line()` (T005) | Baseline capture | One label for both output paths | T006, T012 |\n| `--quiet` parser (T007) | None | `QUIET` set from argv | T008, T011 |\n| Output dispatch (T008) | Formatter, parser | The one-line path | T011, T012 |\n| Verification matrix (T011-T014) | All implementation tasks | Evidence for every AC row | Closure |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n\n1. **T005 add the shared formatter** - 10 minutes - CRITICAL\n2. **T007 parse `--quiet`** - 5 minutes - CRITICAL\n3. **T008 dispatch JSON -> quiet -> text** - 10 minutes - CRITICAL\n4. **T011-T012 line-count and byte-equality checks** - 10 minutes - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: ~35 minutes\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- T003 consumer inventory and T009 help text can run alongside T004-T008\n- T010 error-path check can run as soon as T008 lands\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | Baseline captured | The 16-line, 17-line and 12-line captures exist and match the current script | End of Setup |\n| M2 | Flag works | `--quiet --loc 500 --files 15` prints one line and exits 0 | End of Implementation |\n| M3 | Contract proven | The flag matrix, the byte diff and both regression scripts pass | End of Verification |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n\n### ADR-001: Share one level-line formatter instead of duplicating the label\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: Two output paths must print a byte-identical `Recommended Level:` line. A duplicated `echo` in each path is the obvious implementation and the obvious source of drift: a later label or format change lands in one path only.\n\n**Decision**: Extract `format_level_line()` and call it from both `output_text()` and `output_quiet()`.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- The label has one definition, so byte equality holds by construction rather than by test alone.\n- The script gains one small function, consistent with the helper functions it already defines.\n- `output_text()` changes in source while its output stays identical.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Duplicate the `echo` in `output_quiet()`: rejected because two copies of a parser-visible label drift.\n- Pipe `output_text` through `sed -n '2p'`: rejected because it starts a subprocess, keeps the leading blank line in the pipeline, and breaks if the report's line order changes.\n\n---\n\n### ADR-002: `--json` keeps precedence over `--quiet`\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: Both flags suppress the human report, so a caller can pass both. The pair needs one deterministic meaning.\n\n**Decision**: The output dispatch checks `JSON_OUTPUT` first, then `QUIET`, then falls back to text. `--quiet` is documented as a modifier of the text output only.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- `--json --quiet` prints the unchanged JSON document, so the structured contract never silently downgrades.\n- No new error path or exit code is introduced for a harmless pair.\n- A caller that wants one line must not pass `--json`; the help text and AC-004 make that explicit.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Error on the combination: rejected because it adds a failure mode and a new exit path for a pair with no ambiguity.\n- Let `--quiet` win: rejected because it would replace a structured document with plain text for a caller that asked for JSON.\n\n---\n\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":97,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":88}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/224-deepseek-final2/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_4c42b12fc3844c259c8a8fd5a913b34e","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/224-deepseek-final2/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n<!-- FILL: Keep the prefix table and add the two shell variables this task list uses. GOOD: `S` is the script path. `P` is the packet path. WEAK: Variables are defined below. -->\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n<!-- FILL: Replace the sample tasks with the real setup steps. Each task names a file and a verify command. GOOD: T001 Read the output block in `recommend-level.sh`. Verify: `rg -n 'Recommended Level'` prints one line. WEAK: T001 Set up the project. -->\n\n- [ ] T001 Create project structure\n- [ ] T002 Install dependencies\n- [ ] T003 [P] Configure development tools\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n<!-- FILL: Write one implementation task per file change. Add a `Verify:` line with the command and its expected output. GOOD: T002 Add the `--quiet` branch. Verify: `--quiet` prints one line. WEAK: T002 Implement the feature. -->\n\n- [ ] T004 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 1]\n- [ ] T005 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 2]\n- [ ] T006 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 3]\n- [ ] T007 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Add error handling]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n<!-- FILL: Write one verification task per requirement. Each one runs a command. GOOD: T003 Run both invocations. Verify: `wc -l` prints 1 and 17. WEAK: T003 Test everything. -->\n\n- [ ] T008 Test happy path manually\n- [ ] T009 Test edge cases\n- [ ] T010 Update documentation\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n<!-- FILL: Keep the three completion lines and add the one artifact that proves the phase is done. GOOD: `--quiet` prints one line and the suite passes. WEAK: Work is complete. -->\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n<!-- FILL: Name the spec and plan files. Add the decision record when the packet has one. GOOD: Specification: `spec.md`. Plan: `plan.md`. WEAK: See the other docs. -->\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n<!-- FILL: Fill each checklist section below. -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n<!-- FILL: Keep the three rows and add the rule this packet uses for a blocked task. GOOD: P0 blocks close. P1 needs a recorded reason. WEAK: Follow the priorities. -->\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per setup fact, each with a command. GOOD: CHK-001 [P0] The start commit is in `goal.md` section 4. WEAK: Setup is ready. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in spec.md\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in plan.md\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies identified and available\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per file rule. A command must answer it. GOOD: CHK-010 [P0] `bash -n recommend-level.sh` exits 0. WEAK: Code is clean. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] Code passes lint/format checks\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No console errors or warnings\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] Error handling implemented\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] Code follows project patterns\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per acceptance criterion. GOOD: CHK-020 [P0] `--quiet` prints one line. WEAK: Tests pass. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] Manual testing complete\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] Edge cases tested\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Error scenarios validated\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n<!-- FILL: Keep this section, because every level requires it. Write one check per finding class this packet can produce. Delete only the rows that do not apply, never the section. GOOD: CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Every finding names one class. WEAK: All findings handled. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each actionable finding has a finding class: `instance-only`, `class-of-bug`, `cross-consumer`, `algorithmic`, `matrix/evidence`, or `test-isolation`.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producer inventory completed, or instance-only status proven by grep.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory completed for changed helpers, policies, schema fields, response fields, docs, and tests.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] Security/path/parser/redaction fixes include adversarial table tests for delimiter, joined-input, outside-root, no-op, and fallback cases.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Matrix axes and row count are listed before completion is claimed.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Hostile env/global-state variant executed when tests or code read process-wide state.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-007 [P1] Evidence is pinned to a fix SHA or explicit diff range, not a moving branch-relative range.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per security surface. Write `N/A` with a reason when none applies. GOOD: CHK-030 [P0] The script reads no credential. WEAK: Security is fine. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation implemented\n- [ ] CHK-032 [P1] Auth/authz working correctly\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per document that must agree. GOOD: CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md` and `tasks.md` name the same flag. WEAK: Docs are updated. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] Spec/plan/tasks synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] Code comments adequate\n- [ ] CHK-042 [P2] README updated (if applicable)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per file location rule. GOOD: CHK-050 [P1] Test copies live under `scratch/test/`. WEAK: Files are organized. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Temp files in scratch/ only\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] scratch/ cleaned before completion\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n<!-- FILL: Count the boxes by priority and write the three totals. GOOD: P0 12, P1 13, P2 1. WEAK: Most items done. -->\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | [X] | [ ]/[X] |\n| P1 Items | [Y] | [ ]/[Y] |\n| P2 Items | [Z] | [ ]/[Z] |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-25\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per ADR, or delete the section when the packet records no ADR. GOOD: CHK-100 [P0] ADR-001 is followed by T002. WEAK: Architecture is verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] Architecture decisions documented in decision-record.md\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] All ADRs have status (Proposed/Accepted)\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Alternatives documented with rejection rationale\n- [ ] CHK-103 [P2] Migration path documented (if applicable)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per performance claim, or delete the section when the packet makes none. GOOD: CHK-110 [P1] The flag adds under 5 ms. WEAK: Performance is verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-110 [P1] Response time targets met (NFR-P01)\n- [ ] CHK-111 [P1] Throughput targets met (NFR-P02)\n- [ ] CHK-112 [P2] Load testing completed\n- [ ] CHK-113 [P2] Performance benchmarks documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n## L3+: Deployment Readiness\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per deployment step, or delete the section when the packet ships no service. GOOD: CHK-120 [P0] The rollback command was run in a copy. WEAK: Ready to deploy. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-120 [P0] Rollback procedure documented and tested\n- [ ] CHK-121 [P0] Feature flag configured (if applicable)\n- [ ] CHK-122 [P1] Monitoring/alerting configured\n- [ ] CHK-123 [P1] Runbook created\n- [ ] CHK-124 [P2] Deployment runbook reviewed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n## L3+: Compliance Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per compliance surface, or delete the section when none applies. GOOD: CHK-130 [P1] No license changed. WEAK: Compliance is verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-130 [P1] Security review completed\n- [ ] CHK-131 [P1] Dependency licenses compatible\n- [ ] CHK-132 [P2] OWASP Top 10 checklist completed\n- [ ] CHK-133 [P2] Data handling compliant with requirements\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per document pair that must agree, or delete the section when the packet holds no paired documents. GOOD: CHK-140 [P1] `plan.md` and `tasks.md` agree on the three phases. WEAK: Docs are verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] API documentation complete (if applicable)\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] User-facing documentation updated\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] Knowledge transfer documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Name the real approver for each role. Delete a row when the role does not exist. Write `N/A` or delete the section when no sign-off applies. GOOD: Conductor, runs every task. Operator, merges the commit. WEAK: Signed off. -->\n\n| Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n|----------|------|--------|------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | Technical Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | Product Owner | [ ] Approved | |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | QA Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\n**Variables**: `S` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`. `T` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the output block and the help block in `$S`. Verify: `rg -n 'output_text|show_help' \"$S\"` prints the function definitions and the dispatch use.\n- [ ] T002 Capture the pre-change baseline for both fixtures. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 | wc -l` prints 16, the full-risk variant prints 17, and `--no-recommend-phases` prints 12.\n- [ ] T003 [P] Inventory every in-repo caller and every producer of the label. Verify: `rg -n \"recommend-level.sh\" --glob '!*.md' .` names the two `--json` call sites in `.skilled/commands/speckit/assets/`, and `rg -n \"Recommended Level\" \"$S\"` names one producer.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Add `QUIET=false` to the globals block (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n '^QUIET=false$' \"$S\"` prints one line.\n- [ ] T005 Add `format_level_line()` and call it from `output_text()` (`$S`). Verify: `bash -n \"$S\"` exits 0 and the default output diff against the T002 capture is empty.\n- [ ] T006 Add `output_quiet()`, which calls the formatter once with no leading blank line (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'output_quiet' \"$S\"` prints the definition and the dispatch use.\n- [ ] T007 Parse `--quiet` in the argument loop (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --loc 500 --files 15 | wc -l` prints 1.\n- [ ] T008 Order the dispatch as JSON, then quiet, then text (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --json --quiet --loc 100 --files 3` is byte-identical to the same call without `--quiet`.\n- [ ] T009 Document the flag in the header OPTIONS block, the `show_help` table and one example (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help` names `--quiet` in the options table and in one example.\n- [ ] T010 [P] Confirm no new error path and no stderr change (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --loc 0 --files 0 >/dev/null` exits 1 and writes the existing error to stderr.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T011 Run the flag matrix. Verify: quiet prints 1 line, default prints 16, `--no-recommend-phases` prints 12, and `--json` prints 36.\n- [ ] T012 Compare the two level lines byte for byte. Verify: `diff` between `sed -n '2p'` of the report and the quiet output prints nothing.\n- [ ] T013 Re-run the default and JSON outputs against the T002 capture. Verify: both diffs print nothing.\n- [ ] T014 Check the help text. Verify: `--help` exits 0 and names `--quiet` twice, once in OPTIONS and once in EXAMPLES.\n- [ ] T015 Run the regression scripts (`$T`). Verify: `node \"$T/test-phase-system.js\"` and `node \"$T/test-phase-validation.js\"` both exit 0.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] The artifact that proves it exists: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --loc 500 --files 15 | wc -l` prints 1 and `--json --quiet` matches `--json` alone.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Decision Records**: See ADR-001 and ADR-002 in `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n\nA blocked P0 task stops the phase; a blocked P1 task needs a recorded reason in `implementation-summary.md`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in spec.md. Verify: `rg -c '^\\| REQ-00' spec.md` prints 9.\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in plan.md. Verify: `rg -n 'ADR-001|ADR-002' plan.md` prints both records.\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies available. Verify: `command -v bash wc diff node` names all four.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `bash -n \"$S\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] The script still opens with `set -euo pipefail`. Verify: `rg -n '^set -euo pipefail$' \"$S\"` prints one line.\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] Error handling unchanged: invalid input writes stderr and exits 1. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --loc x --files 1` exits 1.\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] Code follows the file's existing style: lowercase helper names, `output_*` writers, `local` variables.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria met: AC-001 through AC-009.\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] Flag matrix executed: quiet on/off x json on/off x phases on/off.\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] Edge cases tested: empty input, maximum input, both flags together.\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Regression scripts pass: `node \"$T/test-phase-system.js\"` and `node \"$T/test-phase-validation.js\"`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each actionable finding names one class: `instance-only`, `class-of-bug`, `cross-consumer`, `algorithmic`, `matrix/evidence`, or `test-isolation`.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producer inventory completed. Verify: `rg -n \"Recommended Level\" \"$S\"` names every producer, and both go through `format_level_line()`.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory completed. Verify: `rg -n \"recommend-level.sh\" --glob '!*.md' .` names the two YAML call sites and the two test scripts.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] Adversarial cases covered: leading blank line, trailing blank line, both flags, invalid input.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Matrix axes and row count listed before completion is claimed.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Hostile environment variant executed: `env -i PATH=/usr/bin:/bin bash \"$S\" --quiet --loc 500 --files 15`.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-007 [P1] Evidence pinned to a commit SHA or an explicit diff range.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets.\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation unchanged: the numeric checks for `--loc`, `--files` and `--phase-threshold` remain.\n- [ ] CHK-032 [P1] N/A - the script has no auth or authz surface.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md` and `tasks.md` agree on the flag name and the one-line contract.\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The header OPTIONS block and `show_help` both name `--quiet`.\n- [ ] CHK-042 [P2] N/A - the skill README lists the script's purpose, not its option surface.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Temporary captures live under `scratch/` only.\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] `scratch/` cleaned before completion.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | 15 | [ ]/15 |\n| P1 Items | 23 | [ ]/23 |\n| P2 Items | 9 | [ ]/9 |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-25\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] ADR-001 is followed by T005-T006 and ADR-002 by T008.\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] Both ADRs carry a status. Verify: `rg -n '^\\*\\*Status\\*\\*: Accepted' plan.md` prints two lines.\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Alternatives documented with rejection rationale for both ADRs.\n- [ ] CHK-103 [P2] N/A - no data, API or schema migration.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-110 [P1] NFR-P01 holds: `--quiet` adds no subprocess and no file read. Verify: the diff shows only the formatter, the parser case and the dispatch branch.\n- [ ] CHK-111 [P1] NFR-P01 measured: the quiet run and the report run are within measurement noise.\n- [ ] CHK-112 [P2] N/A - a CLI script has no load profile.\n- [ ] CHK-113 [P2] One timing note recorded in `implementation-summary.md`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n## L3+: Deployment Readiness\n\n- [ ] CHK-120 [P0] Rollback procedure documented and rehearsed in a copy.\n- [ ] CHK-121 [P0] N/A - the option is opt-in per invocation, so no feature flag is needed.\n- [ ] CHK-122 [P1] N/A - no service to monitor.\n- [ ] CHK-123 [P1] The `--help` text is the runbook. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help` documents the flag.\n- [ ] CHK-124 [P2] Runbook read back and checked against AC-007.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n## L3+: Compliance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-130 [P1] Security review: the only new input surface is one boolean flag.\n- [ ] CHK-131 [P1] No dependency was added, so no license changed.\n- [ ] CHK-132 [P2] N/A - no web surface, so the OWASP Top 10 does not apply.\n- [ ] CHK-133 [P2] N/A - the script handles no data.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents synchronized. Verify: `validate.sh` reports no placeholder in the four authored docs.\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] N/A - no API; `--help` is the interface.\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] User-facing documentation updated: the `--help` options table and example.\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] Knowledge transfer recorded in ADR-001 and ADR-002.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n\nN/A - single-author packet. The operator who merges the commit approves it; no separate technical lead, product owner or QA lead role exists for this change.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n\n---\n\n## AI EXECUTION PROTOCOL\n\n### Pre-Task Checklist\n\n- [ ] Read `spec.md`, `plan.md` and this file before the first edit.\n- [ ] Confirm the target file is `$S` and nothing else.\n- [ ] Capture the T002 baseline before changing the output block.\n\n### Execution Rules\n\n| Rule | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| TASK-SEQ | Run T001-T003 before T004-T010, and T011-T015 after them. |\n| TASK-SCOPE | Touch `$S` only. Do not edit the README, the YAML call sites or the tests. |\n| TASK-STOP | Stop at the first failing verify command and report the file and line. |\n\n### Status Reporting Format\n\nAfter each task: `T### complete. Files modified: <list>. Verify: <command> -> <observed output>.`\n\n### Blocked Task Protocol\n\nIf a verify command fails twice, mark the task `[B]`, record the command and its output in `implementation-summary.md`, and stop rather than widening scope.\n\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":97,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":87}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/224-deepseek-final2/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
